    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_30a79a528b8e55a7cfc210a9cad12f0fd75ed75488f9d4d199ed6b59c053bc51",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For a compactly supported good kernel already approximable in L2 by dilates of P f, applying V=I-2K_2 preserves compact support while enforcing mean zero. This gives a common tail cutoff, makes Mellin evaluation continuous on the resulting bounded interval, and transfers each zeta zero with 1/2<Re(s)<1 to a zero of f-hat. Combined with universal RH-conditioned necessity, a zero-free f-hat yields the stated RH equivalence.",
