    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_40b20aa9d1139f4ba1a468cf99ec90420fcfa615ea31af5f2ddf8b5ac72e1418",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For a good kernel, P passes through three certified representations: the formal discrete-minus-continuous discrepancy is made well defined almost everywhere by Burnol's absolute-convergence argument, is identified with the multiplicative pseudo-convolution T_{f'}rho_1, and becomes multiplication by zeta after Mellin transformation. The norm and Fubini estimates are the analytic certificates connecting these representations.",
