    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b373d1f12a416dbdafffa9e245f805281689ef9809addd8149fe87f67896c921",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Under RH, the classical approximants to -chi generated by dilates of rho_1 are carried by the bounded dilation-commuting operator T_{f'} to approximants to f generated by dilates of P f: T_{f'}chi=-f and T_{f'}rho_1=P f. Thus the necessity argument transports an existing closure witness to each good kernel rather than recomputing its Gramian.",
